    "result_text": "There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness rejection for owner creation, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and mirroring the existing telephone/household uniqueness checks.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 a single-responsibility create-owner step that, for a present (non-blank) email, scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` when any owner's lower-cased email matches. Skips the check for a missing/blank email (email is optional).\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `DuplicateTelephoneException`).\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, reusing the shared `ProblemDetails.build` helper.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step after `ensureHousehold`, so it runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` has already lower-cased the request's email, keeping the comparison canonical.\n\nThe comparison is robust: the incoming email is already normalized to lower-case by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, and stored emails are lower-cased at compare time, satisfying \"lower-cased email is already used by any other owner.\" Both the new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
